# paper-ink

Full rules: `.opencode/skills/paper-ink/SKILL.md`.
Decision log: `DESIGN.md`. Route markup:
`.opencode/skills/paper-ink/references/route-shapes.md`.

The site is a print hung on washi paper — reflected light, never emitted. If a
change needs a light source, it is out.

## Asserted in `tests/tokens.test.js` — do not tune to pass

- `--color-seal` appears in exactly two kinds of rule: the scope-and-evidence
  convention (`.scope__label`, `.folio__mark`) and interaction
  (`:focus-visible`, `:hover`, `.is-active`, `::selection`). A third kind
  fails the suite.
- `--color-rule` is the ink at 0.18 alpha, never a separate grey.
- ink on washi ≥ 7.0 (AAA); ink-muted and seal ≥ 4.5. `--color-ink-muted`
  has 0.52 of headroom — it breaks invisibly.
- The type scale is 1.25 from `--step--1` up on a 17px body. `--step--2` is
  held off the scale at 0.72rem as a legibility floor.
- `color-scheme: light`, permanently.
- `.atmo` sits below `.print__body`: grain is fibre, ink prints on top.

## Also true, and not asserted

- `--color-washi-deep` is a ground only — ink-muted is 4.38 on it and fails.
- `--color-seal-bright` is decorative, `.seal` only, `aria-hidden`.
- Everything is square. The only radius is 3px on `.seal`.
- Three families and no more: Source Serif 4 (readable), IBM Plex Sans
  (chrome, weight 400 only), IBM Plex Mono (tracked labels and figures, never
  prose, always `tabular-nums` for a year).
- Space is `--space-1`…`--space-6` on a 1.6 ratio. Text sits on
  `--measure-read`, the sheet on `--page-measure`.

## Writing

British English, first person. Carry the scope of a claim in the sentence
after the claim — a number without its qualification does not ship. Label
anything a reader might over-trust (`Self-reported dates`,
`Unreviewed preprint`, `Teammate-reported`) in the mono label at
`--color-ink-muted`.

## Never

Glow, bloom, blur, smooth gradients, wet reflections, chrome or bevelled type,
shadows, elevation, a fourth accent, an icon, an emoji, a hero image above a
title, a vanity metric, a dark-mode toggle, or a colour picked by eye.
